  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="5373b3a3-4e79-5d23-a2d1-1dd7f2be57c2" activityNameId="903d5998-20a8-52ce-b927-af7ab05fb468" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Carbon dioxide compression, transport and storage</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Carbon dioxide compression, transport and storage
The CO2 flow is compressed through a compressor to 11 MPa and then transported through a pipeline to the storage site. The length of the transport pipeline is assumed to be 50 km. At the storage site, the CO2 will be further compressed to 15 MPa and injected into a geological reservoir through wells with a depth of 3 km each. 

Source: Koornneef, J., van Keulen, T., Faaij, A. &amp; Turkenburg, W. Life cycle assessment of a pulverized coal
UUID: df1d4e3c-8c25-4b6d-8d2b-52d9abd4ab13
Location: 
Technology: 
Time period: 
Production volume: 
Sampling: Sampling procedure: Literature data
Extrapolations: 
Uncertainty adjustments: 
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_df1d4e3c-8c25-4b6d-8d2b-52d9abd4ab13.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
